{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 8.364,
   "text": "I clean a little dance studio downtown, after the last class goes home."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 8.964,
   "end": 13.743,
   "text": "One whole wall is mirror. And the owner, Miss Adele, gave me one rule."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 14.343,
   "end": 19.655,
   "text": "Never turn off the lights while you're facing the mirror. Always turn your back to it first."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 20.455,
   "end": 23.911,
   "text": "I figured she was worried I'd trip in the dark."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 24.611,
   "end": 29.304,
   "text": "For a whole year, I did it her way. Back to the glass. Click. Out the door."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 30.104,
   "end": 35.416,
   "text": "Then last night, my phone buzzed just as I reached for the switch... and I forgot."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 36.416,
   "end": 40.107,
   "text": "The lights went out. I was staring straight into the glass."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 41.107,
   "end": 44.435,
   "text": "And in the dark, I heard it. Tap. Tap. Tap."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 45.235,
   "end": 48.925,
   "text": "Like ballet shoes... on the other side of the mirror."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 51.525,
   "end": 53.957,
   "text": "I slapped the lights back on."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 54.957,
   "end": 59.075,
   "text": "There was my reflection. Same mop. Same tired face."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 59.875,
   "end": 64.141,
   "text": "But it moved a half second after I did. Every single time."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 65.741,
   "end": 68.664,
   "text": "I didn't finish mopping. I just left."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start": 70.064,
   "end": 77.275,
   "text": "This morning, Miss Adele called me. She asked why I came back at three a.m.... and danced in the dark until sunrise."
  }
 ],
